    "run_completed_partial_refusals": {
      "_doc": "Partial run whose ingest stage refused three files: 5 of 8 recordings reached a session. Locks the shape refusals actually take on the wire, which no earlier scenario covered at all. Three things are pinned here. (a) `reason` on Cause — the UnusableReason discriminator the desktop localises from (`desktop.pipeline.diagnostic.reason.<value>`); before it existed the popover rendered the English `message` raw in all 21 non-en locales. (b) The `ingest` bucket carrying failures while `outcome` is still `completed` — a refusal is outcome 2 of the taxonomy in docs/design-analysis-lifecycle.md §5.1, a pass, and must never read as a dead run. (c) The last entry deliberately omits `reason` entirely, reproducing an event written by a sidecar older than Aug 2026: both sides must fall back to `message` rather than fail the decode or blank the row.",
